<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Krbava Field</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1493">1493</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-ottoman-wars">Croatian–Ottoman wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Krbava Field was fought on 9 September 1493 on the Krbava plain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lika">Lika</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, between a Croatian army under Ban Emerik Derenčin and Ottoman raiders led by Hadım Yakub Pasha. The Croatian nobility suffered a heavy defeat: the ban was captured and many nobles were killed. The disaster opened Croatia to further Ottoman raids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-krbava-field.jpg" alt="Battle of Krbava Field" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leonhard Beck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Krbava_Field.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
